WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.131 --> 00:00:02.330
- Your new book I mean, as a fellow Texan,

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.582
there could not be a
better title for a Texan.

00:00:04.582 --> 00:00:05.415
(laughs)

00:00:05.415 --> 00:00:06.740
- Your memoir is called open book.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:07.573
- Yes.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:09.490
- And is this like hard,

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:10.630
'cause normally I would ask people.

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:12.080
What was your hardest to
share personal stories,

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.440
but I feel like we might be similar

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.927
and it's almost cathartic.

00:00:14.927 --> 00:00:16.510
- You have no filter, like ...

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:17.750
- I have no filter.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:18.583
- I don't neither.

00:00:18.583 --> 00:00:19.540
- I've never had a filter.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.373
- Me neither.

00:00:20.373 --> 00:00:21.860
- I think it's very important

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:22.810
just to be yourself.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:23.900
And that's what's authentic.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:25.329
And that's what people love about you.

00:00:25.329 --> 00:00:26.162
(audience applauds)
- Yeah, I think that's

00:00:26.162 --> 00:00:28.630
love about you, if
you're very honest.And...

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.490
- I'm very honest.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:30.460
- Especially in this book,

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:32.240
you open up about some
pretty personal stuff,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.073
that's hard to get through.

00:00:33.073 --> 00:00:34.710
And most people I feel like

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.220
would be afraid to say
that in the public eye,

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.680
but I think it's so brave of you

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.990
and so cool of you and strong of you,

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:41.410
because one, when you address that,

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.350
then you know you're
actually getting past it.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.630
You are working through it.
- Yeah and definitely

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.710
like my openness holds me accountable.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:52.710
And for me, when I decided to get sober,

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.370
I stopped drinking

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.450
and I just had so much clarity,

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.410
that with my openness, was just like

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.580
I started learning so much about myself

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.020
and why I had to drink

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:06.600
to try and escape

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.963
and try and just feel, just normal,

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.130
I thought it was helping with my anxiety

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.910
and it was actually making it worse.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:15.743
- Yeah, 'cause people will say that,

00:01:15.743 --> 00:01:16.576
they are like,

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.409
"Oh, it's calming."

00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:18.400
They say that all the
time. We find all of...

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.930
- [Jessica Simpson] It's
absolutely not calming.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.090
- I know, but I just
think its brave of you

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.790
to come out and say that

00:01:25.276 --> 00:01:26.109
and has it been rewarding?

00:01:26.109 --> 00:01:26.942
Like getting it out?

00:01:26.942 --> 00:01:28.560
- It has, it's been unbelievable.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.560
I've been on this book tour

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.560
and every City that I'm going into,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.490
these people that come up to me,

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.617
they're like, "I'm gonna be sober",

00:01:39.596 --> 00:01:41.567
"I wanna tell you first"

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.430
"before I tell my family and my parents."

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:45.640
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah,
and it's connection.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.050
- Yeah, it's a really deep connection.

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.970
And then I've had mothers come up to me

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:54.490
and thanking me and they're
not afraid of therapy.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:55.323
For some reason...

00:01:55.323 --> 00:01:56.156
- Why are people afraid of that?

00:01:56.156 --> 00:01:56.989
- People are so afraid of...

00:01:56.989 --> 00:01:57.822
- I am in therapy. I love therapy.

00:01:57.822 --> 00:02:00.760
- I know I love therapy.
it's like no judgment.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.150
- Yeah, you can say whatever you want.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:02.983
They're not in your circle.

00:02:02.983 --> 00:02:03.816
- [Jessica Simpson] No.

00:02:03.816 --> 00:02:04.649
- You will not be judged.

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:05.482
- You Will not be judged.

00:02:05.482 --> 00:02:06.315
- And even if you are, you don't know 'em,

00:02:06.315 --> 00:02:07.148
you're paying them its fine.

00:02:07.148 --> 00:02:07.981
(audience laughs)

00:02:07.981 --> 00:02:08.814
- Yeah, exactly.

00:02:08.814 --> 00:02:09.718
- I'm paying you to listen to this.

00:02:09.718 --> 00:02:10.551
(laughs)

00:02:10.551 --> 00:02:11.384
- They are not your friends.

00:02:11.384 --> 00:02:12.217
My therapist at the very beginning.

00:02:12.217 --> 00:02:13.160
I was like, Oh my gosh,

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:14.310
I feel like we're best friends.

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:16.447
And she goes, "I wanna make it very clear"

00:02:16.447 --> 00:02:17.603
"that we're not friends."

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:19.559
(audience laughs)

00:02:19.559 --> 00:02:21.870
- (laughs) And I was like,

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:24.051
I don't know if anybody
has ever said that, to me.

00:02:24.051 --> 00:02:24.950
(laughs)

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.160
- I wanna make this very clear,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.270
I don't wanna be your friends.

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:29.536
- We are not friends.

00:02:29.536 --> 00:02:30.453
(laughs)

00:02:30.453 --> 00:02:31.567
- I love your therapist.

